{"name":"Lima Bean","hex":"#e1d590","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"lima bean","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["Any of species Phaseolus lunatus of bean-bearing plants.","Fruit of this plant."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/lima_bean"}],"entries":[{"title":"Lima bean","blocks":[{"text":"A lima bean, also commonly known as butter bean, sieva bean, double bean or Madagascar bean, is a legume grown for its edible seeds or beans."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/9b/Phaseoulus_lunatus.jpg/330px-Phaseoulus_lunatus.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Lima_bean","wikidata":"Q1166136"},{"title":"Lima","blocks":[{"text":"Lima is the capital and largest city of Peru, as well as a primate city. It is located in the valleys of the Chillón, Rímac and Lurín Rivers, in the desert zone of the central coastal part of the country, overlooking the Pacific Ocean. The city is considered the political, cultural, financial and commercial center of Peru. Jurisdictionally, the metropolis extends mainly within the province of Lima and in a smaller portion, to the west, within the Constitutional Province of Callao, where the seaport and the Jorge Chávez Airport are located. Both provinces have had regional autonomy since 2002."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/69/Bas%C3%ADlica_Catedral_Metropolitana_de_Lima_%28cropped%29.jpg/330px-Bas%C3%ADlica_Catedral_Metropolitana_de_Lima_%28cropped%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Lima","wikidata":"Q2868"},{"title":"Bean","blocks":[{"text":"A bean is the seed of plants in many genera of the legume family (Fabaceae) used as a vegetable for human consumption or animal feed. The seeds are sold fresh or preserved through drying (a pulse). Beans have been cultivated since the seventh millennium BCE in Thailand, and since the second millennium BCE in Europe and in Peru. Most beans, with the exception of peas, are summer crops. As legumes, the plants fix nitrogen and form seeds with a high protein content. They are produced on a scale of millions of tons annually in many countries, with India as the largest producer."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/a0/French_beans_J1.JPG/330px-French_beans_J1.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Bean","wikidata":"Q379813"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/b2/Lima_beans_in_an_illustrated_catalogue_of_seeds_%281894%29_%2817802859704%29.jpg/500px-Lima_beans_in_an_illustrated_catalogue_of_seeds_%281894%29_%2817802859704%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/b2/Lima_beans_in_an_illustrated_catalogue_of_seeds_%281894%29_%2817802859704%29.jpg/1280px-Lima_beans_in_an_illustrated_catalogue_of_seeds_%281894%29_%2817802859704%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/b2/Lima_beans_in_an_illustrated_catalogue_of_seeds_%281894%29_%2817802859704%29.jpg/500px-Lima_beans_in_an_illustrated_catalogue_of_seeds_%281894%29_%2817802859704%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Lima beans in a seed catalogue, 1894","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ALima_beans_in_an_illustrated_catalogue_of_seeds_(1894)_(17802859704).jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/eb/Speckled_butterbeans.jpg/330px-Speckled_butterbeans.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/eb/Speckled_butterbeans.jpg/960px-Speckled_butterbeans.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipe